# CKS Exam Drill: Host System Hardening & Footprint Reduction

System hardening focuses on minimizing the host OS attack surface, restricting network exposure, securing permissions on critical Kubernetes files, and auditing running services.

---

## 1. Network & Port Hardening

Identify open TCP and UDP listening sockets:

```bash
sudo ss -tulpn
# or
sudo lsof -i -P -n | grep LISTEN
```

Standard Kubernetes port assignments:

| Port | Component | Host |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`6443`** | Kubernetes API Server | Control Plane |
| **`2379–2380`** | etcd server client / peer API | Control Plane |
| **`10250`** | Kubelet API | All Nodes |
| **`10257`** | kube-controller-manager | Control Plane |
| **`10259`** | kube-scheduler | Control Plane |
| **`30000–32767`** | NodePort Services range | Worker Nodes |

---

## 2. Managing Services & Reducing OS Footprint

Audit active services:

```bash
systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running
```

Disable unneeded or unauthorized services:

```bash
sudo systemctl stop <service-name>
sudo systemctl disable <service-name>
```

Audit and remove unnecessary packages:

```bash
sudo apt purge -y <unneeded-package>
sudo apt autoremove -y
```

---

## 3. CIS Recommended Kubernetes File Permissions

| Path | Recommended Permissions | Recommended Owner |
| :--- | :---: | :---: |
| `/etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml` | `0600` or `0644` | `root:root` |
| `/etc/kubernetes/*.conf` (`admin.conf`, etc.) | `0600` | `root:root` |
| `/etc/kubernetes/pki/*.key` | `0600` | `root:root` |
| `/etc/kubernetes/pki/*.crt` | `0644` | `root:root` |
| `/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml` | `0600` or `0644` | `root:root` |

To fix permissions:

```bash
sudo chmod 600 /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf
sudo chmod 600 /etc/kubernetes/pki/*.key
sudo chmod 644 /etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml
sudo chown -R root:root /etc/kubernetes/
```

